[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2100847151","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/17305#issuecomment-2100847151","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/17305","id":2100847151,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M59OGIv","user":{"login":"benvanik","id":75337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik","html_url":"https://github.com/benvanik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-08T15:29:14Z","updated_at":"2024-05-08T15:29:14Z","body":"You're changing the ABI and inducing undefined behavior :)\r\nYou cannot change the function interface after the dispatch has been formed. A flow.dispatch *must* be consistent with the target of the dispatch (in this case, your function).","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2100847151/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2100850171","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/17305#issuecomment-2100850171","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/17305","id":2100850171,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M59OG37","user":{"login":"benvanik","id":75337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik","html_url":"https://github.com/benvanik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-08T15:30:44Z","updated_at":"2024-05-08T15:30:44Z","body":"(the technical detail here is that ROCM takes all buffers and other arguments as a packed struct, and if you change the order/counts of any input that struct layout changes - if you pass a struct in one layout from the caller to the callee expecting a different layout you'll get garbage)","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2100850171/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2100857321","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/17305#issuecomment-2100857321","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/17305","id":2100857321,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M59OInp","user":{"login":"martin-luecke","id":16363540,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzYzNTQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16363540?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/martin-luecke","html_url":"https://github.com/martin-luecke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martin-luecke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martin-luecke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martin-luecke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martin-luecke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martin-luecke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martin-luecke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martin-luecke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martin-luecke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martin-luecke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-08T15:34:17Z","updated_at":"2024-05-08T15:34:17Z","body":"When I remove the input I change the dispatch as well, so without the input my dispatch looks like this:\r\n```\r\n  func.func @isolated_benchmark() -> tensor<128x128xf32> {\r\n    %2 = flow.dispatch @func::@func() : () -> tensor<128x128xf32>\r\n    return %2 : tensor<128x128xf32>\r\n  }\r\n```\r\nWhen I change the layout of inputs, without adjusting the dispatch I get an error about the type mismatch as expected.\r\n\r\nOr are you referring to another portion of the code?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2100857321/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2100864882","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/17305#issuecomment-2100864882","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/17305","id":2100864882,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M59OKdy","user":{"login":"benvanik","id":75337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik","html_url":"https://github.com/benvanik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-08T15:38:11Z","updated_at":"2024-05-08T15:38:11Z","body":"Not sure I'm following.\r\n\r\nThe rule is: the dispatch and the dispatchee must match exactly. Making that true can be tricky when mixing layers of the stack (stream and flow are two different layers), which is why the inline dispatch region ops (flow.dispatch.region and flow.dispatch.workgroups) exist as they take care of everything for you and lower properly.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2100864882/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2100884095","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/17305#issuecomment-2100884095","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/i